WEBVTT

00:04.830 --> 00:06.630
Shoot! I'm late, I'm late!

00:12.600 --> 00:14.570
Looks like I made it just in time.

00:22.810 --> 00:24.780
What a weird girl.

00:25.650 --> 00:26.580
Yo, Mizuki.

00:27.290 --> 00:29.450
I almost didn't make it on time.

00:30.120 --> 00:31.050
What?

00:31.760 --> 00:33.730
Mizuki? Not...quite?

00:34.190 --> 00:37.720
Well, you didn't wake up when I went to get you this morning, Hiroyuki.

00:38.160 --> 00:39.860
Hiroyuki? Who's that?

00:40.770 --> 00:42.230
You're just hopeless, Hiroyuki.

00:42.530 --> 00:43.370
Huh?

00:43.370 --> 00:45.600
Really, that's so like you, Hiro.

00:46.400 --> 00:49.970
No, wait, I'm Kazuki!
Right, I'm Kazuki Sendou!

00:50.410 --> 00:51.900
Are you okay, Hiroyuki?

00:52.810 --> 00:54.250
You're just hopeless, Hiroyuki.

00:54.380 --> 00:57.580
N-no! My name is Kazuki Sendou!

00:57.850 --> 01:00.090
And the person sitting there is Mizuki Takase,

01:00.090 --> 01:01.520
whom I've known since middle school!

01:01.920 --> 01:03.950
Hey, who's this Mizuki person, Hiro?

01:04.390 --> 01:06.950
Hiroyuki, your name isn't Kazuki, you know?

01:08.030 --> 01:09.460
You're just hopeless, Hiroyuki.

01:09.830 --> 01:10.660
No...

01:10.960 --> 01:12.230
No!

01:15.630 --> 01:17.030
That's not right!

01:17.470 --> 01:20.440
Oh, Hiroyuki, I finished cleaning.

01:21.210 --> 01:22.730
No!

01:23.510 --> 01:24.240
Hiro!

01:24.240 --> 01:25.180
Hiroyuki?

01:25.980 --> 01:27.310
You're just hopeless, Hiroyuki.

01:27.650 --> 01:28.700
Hiroyuki.

01:29.080 --> 01:31.910
I'm... I'm... I'm...

01:32.420 --> 01:35.320
Kazuki Sendou!

01:38.090 --> 01:39.320
Mizuki?

01:40.090 --> 01:42.580
Where am I? Who am I?

01:43.430 --> 01:47.300
Don't start that dumb act so early in the morning!

01:50.770 --> 01:54.330
<i>Just be you and don't change.</i>
<i>Kimi no Mama de Kawaranaide</i>

01:54.870 --> 01:58.010
<i>You're more precious to me than anyone.</i>
<i>Dare Yori mo Taisetsu na</i>

01:58.010 --> 02:01.570
<i>You have a great, sparkling dream...</i>
<i>Ohki na Yume Kagayakaseta</i>

02:01.780 --> 02:04.840
<i>...and you're my one and only friend.</i>
<i>Tada Hitori no Tomodachi</i>

02:05.120 --> 02:08.720
<i>Nani o Shite mo Tsutawarazu</i>

02:05.120 --> 02:06.990
<i>It just doesn't get across...</i>

02:06.990 --> 02:08.720
<i>...no matter what you do.</i>

02:08.720 --> 02:12.290
<i>It's just not working right at all.</i>
<i>Umaku Ikanai Bakari de</i>

02:12.290 --> 02:15.660
<i>But even I and everyone else...</i>
<i>Watashi Datte Dare Datte</i>

02:15.860 --> 02:19.390
<i>... have times like that.</i>
<i>Atarimae ni Aru Koto</i>

02:19.460 --> 02:22.870
<i>Those things that don't return to your heart.</i>
<i>Mune no Naka ni Kaeranai</i>

02:23.070 --> 02:26.470
<i>But even those words and feelings...</i>
<i>Omoi mo Kotoba mo Itsuka</i>

02:26.640 --> 02:31.040
<i>... will come back in time someday...</i>
<i>Jikan ga Tateba Modotte Kuru kara</i>

02:31.240 --> 02:34.180
<i>... before you know it.</i>
<i>Shiranai Uchi ni</i>

02:34.480 --> 02:40.390
<i>There's only one thing you can do right now.</i>
<i>Ima Kimiga Dekiru Koto wa Hitotsu</i>

02:40.750 --> 02:47.450
<i>Just accept it and go with it.</i>
<i>Sono Mama Ukeirete Yukou</i>

02:48.130 --> 02:52.130
<i>Just be you and stay true to yourself.</i>
<i>Kimi no Mama de Itsuwarazu ni</i>

02:52.130 --> 02:55.300
<i>Take a little break.</i>
<i>Sukoshi Hitoyasumi Shite</i>

02:55.300 --> 02:59.040
<i>Take your impatience and your hardships...</i>
<i>Aseru Kimochi Kurushii Koto</i>

02:59.040 --> 03:02.300
<i>...and turn them into your strengths.</i>
<i>Kimi no Power ni Kaete</i>

03:02.370 --> 03:06.140
<i>Just be you and don't change.</i>
<i>Kimi no Mama de Kawaranaide</i>

03:06.510 --> 03:09.610
<i>You're more precious to me than anyone.</i>
<i>Dare Yori mo Taisetsu na</i>

03:09.610 --> 03:13.210
<i>You have a great, sparkling dream...</i>
<i>Ohki na Yume Kagayakaseta</i>

03:13.420 --> 03:16.320
<i>...and you're my one and only friend.</i>
<i>Tada Hitori no Tomodachi</i>

03:19.360 --> 03:26.030
FATEFUL FIRST
EXPERIENCE?!

03:27.170 --> 03:30.140
I'm so sorry. You're always coming to wake up Kazuki.

03:30.240 --> 03:31.900
I've been doing it for so long, I'm used to it.

03:34.540 --> 03:37.670
I feel like I had some kind of weird dream, but...

03:37.810 --> 03:39.280
What was it about?

03:39.640 --> 03:40.770
Oh, well.

03:41.850 --> 03:43.450
We're gonna be late if we don't hurry up!

03:43.450 --> 03:45.850
Hey, who's the one that overslept?!

03:54.860 --> 03:56.050
"Yoyomori Station"

04:01.730 --> 04:03.760
You look a little out of shape.

04:04.740 --> 04:06.600
Maybe I've been studying too much for entrance exams.

04:07.010 --> 04:08.100
No way!

04:08.210 --> 04:09.070
Of course not.

04:09.140 --> 04:10.800
Our school automatically gets us into college, after all.

04:10.880 --> 04:11.770
Sheesh.

04:14.450 --> 04:15.470
This voice...

04:16.080 --> 04:19.410
Exactly, our high school most definitely gets us into college.

04:19.650 --> 04:21.140
We may be starting our senior year tomorrow,

04:21.220 --> 04:23.350
but we have no worries about the future whatsoever!

04:28.790 --> 04:31.130
But are you fine with that?!

04:31.130 --> 04:34.860
Can you be satisfied with just letting those peaceful days go by?!

04:35.400 --> 04:38.460
My brother! And my sister!

04:39.600 --> 04:41.440
Hey, Mom, that person's weird.

04:41.510 --> 04:42.970
Shh, don't look at him.

04:43.210 --> 04:45.440
Young people these days are just so...

04:46.340 --> 04:48.140
Wanna go home, Mizuki?

04:48.280 --> 04:50.010
Y-yeah, let's.

04:53.180 --> 04:56.020
My brother! And my sister!

04:56.690 --> 04:58.050
The appointed place...

04:58.160 --> 05:00.820
...and the appointed time is precisely here and now.

05:01.130 --> 05:02.490
Where are you going?

05:02.490 --> 05:04.020
Where are you going?!

05:04.500 --> 05:05.830
Did they have a fight?

05:05.230 --> 05:06.600
Are those two even related?

05:06.600 --> 05:07.900
There's a girl, too.

05:10.170 --> 05:13.070
So, where are you dragging us off to so early in the morning?

05:13.740 --> 05:15.540
Do not let the details bother you.

05:15.740 --> 05:18.010
Only think of our destiny.

05:19.380 --> 05:21.870
Looks like Taishi's quirky side is acting up again.

05:21.980 --> 05:23.450
If it weren't for that...

05:24.050 --> 05:25.520
But why Odaiba?

05:25.620 --> 05:27.920
Have they built something interesting over there?

05:28.220 --> 05:29.380
I don't know.

05:36.260 --> 05:38.230
Wh-what the heck is this?!

05:50.440 --> 05:53.070
It looks like it goes on for miles.

05:53.580 --> 05:55.240
How many thousands of people are there?

05:55.310 --> 05:56.910
It's too soon to be surprised.

05:56.980 --> 05:58.970
This is only the tip of the iceberg.

05:59.350 --> 06:02.220
It is merely the entrance to
Hades, where Cerberus awaits.

06:02.690 --> 06:03.680
But what...

06:03.790 --> 06:05.380
...is this line for?

06:09.230 --> 06:10.820
Now, let us go, comrades!

06:11.100 --> 06:12.930
Kazuki! And Mizuki!

06:13.830 --> 06:16.390
The festival of anime, comics, and games!

06:16.530 --> 06:18.900
The center of swirling ambition, love, and hatred!

06:19.400 --> 06:21.770
Yes, to the doujinshi exhibition and spot sale!

06:22.210 --> 06:23.470
Doujinshi?!

06:23.540 --> 06:24.740
Exhibition and spot sale?!

06:38.790 --> 06:40.620
Mizuki, where are you?!

06:41.830 --> 06:43.820
I'm gonna get crushed by meat buns!

06:44.730 --> 06:46.320
Over here! Over here!

06:51.570 --> 06:54.800
Wait a minute, Taishi! How come you can walk so normally?!

06:54.910 --> 06:57.140
Hey, I heard there's a
KSS industry booth!

06:56.810 --> 06:58.010
Hurry, hurry, hurry!

06:57.680 --> 06:59.410
I think it's limited to 3000 units!

07:03.950 --> 07:05.210
Hey, Mizuki?

07:06.180 --> 07:08.920
Comrade Mizuki, you'll get stepped on if you lie on the floor.

07:09.550 --> 07:10.990
I've had enough!

07:10.990 --> 07:12.720
It's hot and it's smelly and it's noisy!

07:12.720 --> 07:14.560
You're admitting defeat already, my comrade?

07:13.220 --> 07:14.560
I hate it, I hate it!

07:14.630 --> 07:18.290
Not "already"! We waited in line for three hours to get in!

07:18.500 --> 07:20.000
I'm going home,
I'm going home, I'm going home,

07:20.000 --> 07:20.990
I'm going home, I'm going home!

07:23.700 --> 07:25.640
The author's selling it herself!

07:31.210 --> 07:32.580
Hey, Mizuki!

07:33.810 --> 07:34.870
It's no use!

07:35.010 --> 07:38.110
If you get separated in this veritable maze of a convention hall,

07:38.620 --> 07:42.850
the probability of finding each other is less than 0.00008%.

07:43.350 --> 07:44.520
But still...

07:44.520 --> 07:47.250
No matter, we can just look around by ourselves.

07:48.160 --> 07:50.420
Yes, as our first step for the sake of our ambition.

07:51.100 --> 07:52.060
Ambition?

07:52.130 --> 07:53.760
Now, come on!

07:54.430 --> 07:55.300
Taishi! Hey!

07:59.770 --> 08:00.570
But...

08:02.010 --> 08:03.710
...no matter where I go...

08:03.240 --> 08:04.410
"I am out"

08:03.240 --> 08:04.410
Sorry, please

08:03.240 --> 08:04.410
come again

08:04.410 --> 08:05.840
"To Heart"

08:04.410 --> 08:05.840
End of line

08:08.580 --> 08:11.280
...it's people, people, and more people.

08:12.420 --> 08:13.650
Hey, Taishi?!

08:24.460 --> 08:27.590
Good grief, why are there so many people?

08:27.700 --> 08:29.690
And all the books look about the same, no matter where I look.

08:30.540 --> 08:31.970
I just don't get it.

08:32.340 --> 08:33.930
I think I'll go home already.

08:35.340 --> 08:37.470
Please wait a moment

08:38.410 --> 08:40.740
Noooo!

08:41.480 --> 08:42.580
No!

08:42.580 --> 08:45.020
Someone please stop me!

08:46.350 --> 08:46.980
What?

08:46.980 --> 08:48.040
Noooo!

08:54.460 --> 08:55.980
Ow!

08:59.200 --> 09:00.360
Are you okay?

09:02.200 --> 09:04.770
You have just saved my life!

09:04.770 --> 09:05.340
Huh?

09:05.340 --> 09:07.500
You stopped my runaway cart.

09:08.140 --> 09:09.510
Thank you, thank you.
It was just a coincidence...

09:09.510 --> 09:10.540
Oh, no!

09:10.540 --> 09:11.380
What?

09:10.910 --> 09:13.500
I have to deliver the books to my customers.

09:13.880 --> 09:16.640
Well, goodbye, my lifesaver.

09:25.290 --> 09:26.950
I wonder if I can get out this way?

09:27.060 --> 09:29.460
Excuse me, that's an emergency exit!

09:29.460 --> 09:30.690
What? Me?

09:30.960 --> 09:35.130
That door is to be kept closed, so please use the designated exits.

09:35.400 --> 09:37.330
Oh, I'm so sorry.

09:37.870 --> 09:41.530
Okay, please don't run inside the convention hall!

09:41.640 --> 09:45.630
Oh, you in the costume, long weapons aren't allowed.

09:45.780 --> 09:48.010
Please do that in the cosplay hall!

09:49.580 --> 09:52.640
Which means, I have to go through all that again.

09:56.120 --> 09:57.850
Is the exit that way?

09:57.960 --> 09:59.120
What the heck are ya sayin'?!

09:59.590 --> 10:01.490
Hurry up, I want it already.

10:01.730 --> 10:03.390
You don't have that many copies,

10:03.460 --> 10:06.130
so it's more efficient if you distribute it now.

10:06.130 --> 10:09.260
"Karamitei"

10:06.500 --> 10:09.260
So, like I said, when I'm distributin' is written right here!

10:09.870 --> 10:13.170
Sure, I could jump the gun, but that would affect people's trust in me!

10:13.370 --> 10:16.670
Trying to act so cool, when you have people lining up for once.

10:17.210 --> 10:18.640
What'd you say?!

10:18.640 --> 10:20.640
Here I'm tryin' to be nice, and you try to walk all over me!

10:21.380 --> 10:23.940
I'm cancelin'! I'm cancelin' distributin' my new issue!

10:24.880 --> 10:26.440
You're being unreasonable!

10:26.880 --> 10:29.820
I, Yuu Inagawa, may forget the way of humanity,

10:29.890 --> 10:32.880
but I have never once forgotten the honor among doujin!

10:33.190 --> 10:37.390
Is that to say we lack a doujin's honor?!

10:37.730 --> 10:39.420
We can't let you get away with saying that.

10:43.570 --> 10:45.500
Oh, sorry. Is the exit...

10:45.970 --> 10:47.710
Are you trying to get in our way?!

10:47.710 --> 10:50.000
N-no, I'm just looking for...

10:50.310 --> 10:51.300
That's it!

10:52.180 --> 10:54.580
This guy is none other than the man known and feared...

10:54.580 --> 10:57.810
...around the Shinsekai area as Sabu the Savage Dog!

10:57.880 --> 10:58.880
What?

10:58.880 --> 11:00.650
It is cowardly to get reinforcements.

11:00.720 --> 11:02.240
Cowardly, shmowardly!

11:03.020 --> 11:04.820
No, I'm telling you, I...

11:06.820 --> 11:10.430
You there! Please stop this violence at once!

11:10.430 --> 11:11.960
Th-this is bad!

11:11.960 --> 11:13.330
This is too dangerous!

11:13.400 --> 11:14.960
Run! Run!

11:17.340 --> 11:19.130
We're gonna get outta here for now, too!

11:19.200 --> 11:20.140
What?

11:21.070 --> 11:22.900
We'll come back when things've cooled down!

11:40.560 --> 11:43.650
You sure came by at a lucky time for me. You've got my thanks.

11:45.000 --> 11:46.730
I finally made it outside.

11:47.030 --> 11:49.400
What? You already found the books you wanted?

11:50.400 --> 11:52.030
It isn't like that.

11:57.170 --> 11:58.770
What are you? A moron?

11:58.910 --> 11:59.710
What?

11:59.810 --> 12:03.180
There's no way you'll get a connection so easily in a place like this.

12:05.050 --> 12:06.680
You're an amateur at this, aren't you?

12:07.620 --> 12:11.060
Amateur nothing, this is the first time I've been to one of these.

12:11.390 --> 12:12.760
One of these?!

12:12.990 --> 12:15.050
Man, it's just like Mizuki said.

12:15.760 --> 12:18.200
It's hot, and it's smelly, and it's noisy.

12:18.560 --> 12:21.000
I don't get why so many people are gathered here.

12:21.070 --> 12:22.360
You freakin' moron!

12:22.900 --> 12:23.870
Wha?!

12:23.500 --> 12:25.130
Just shut up and try readin' this!

12:30.470 --> 12:33.030
I feel like I've seen this somewhere before...

12:33.810 --> 12:34.900
Well?

12:45.390 --> 12:47.190
What're ya laughin' at me for?!

12:47.360 --> 12:49.260
Looks like you don't value your life very much!

12:49.560 --> 12:53.120
No, no, it's funny.

12:53.600 --> 12:55.500
F-for real?!

12:55.630 --> 12:57.160
Yeah, honest.

12:57.700 --> 12:58.900
Then, there's more.

12:58.970 --> 12:59.840
What?

12:59.840 --> 13:01.140
Come with me.

13:02.910 --> 13:06.400
I'll teach ya what a doujinshi exhibition and spot sale is all about!

13:09.150 --> 13:10.640
Teach me?

13:10.820 --> 13:13.150
But I just finally got outside.

13:13.780 --> 13:15.280
Details, details.

13:16.820 --> 13:18.520
Where have you been?

13:18.720 --> 13:21.330
Could it be you were crying your eyes out in the bathroom...

13:21.330 --> 13:22.620
...because your sales were just so horrible?

13:23.160 --> 13:24.790
Oh, it's you.

13:25.100 --> 13:28.000
I completely sold out during the morning,

13:28.000 --> 13:29.800
so I'm empty-handed and on my way home.

13:29.870 --> 13:31.170
Is she your friend?

13:31.170 --> 13:32.840
We'll call her that for now,

13:32.840 --> 13:34.640
though I'd like to wash my hands of her, already.

13:34.940 --> 13:37.030
Wh-what?! You're just a panda anyway!

13:37.510 --> 13:39.310
Panda! Panda! Panda! Panda!

13:39.610 --> 13:42.310
Pandas should go back to the mountains of Kobe!

13:42.810 --> 13:45.810
I'm going back to the city.

13:46.780 --> 13:48.980
Oh, how easy!

13:49.250 --> 13:51.850
Empty-handed! Empty-handed!
Empty-handed! Empty-handed!

13:51.990 --> 13:53.550
Who was that?

13:53.790 --> 13:56.630
That's Eimi Ohba, of a group called "Cat or Fish".

13:56.630 --> 13:58.300
She's not worth rememberin',

13:58.300 --> 14:00.320
though she does seem to be popular.

14:01.500 --> 14:02.520
Now!

14:02.600 --> 14:03.800
Now?

14:04.170 --> 14:06.070
Why does this happen to me?

14:06.070 --> 14:10.030
Karamitei

14:06.540 --> 14:10.030
My group's got decent name-recognition back in Kansai.

14:10.640 --> 14:13.300
Unfortunately, it's a tiny group with only me in it.

14:13.480 --> 14:17.040
'Sides, if you stay here, you might be able find your friend, right?

14:17.820 --> 14:19.440
Well, that's true, but...

14:19.720 --> 14:21.280
I'd like this, please.

14:21.420 --> 14:24.480
Oh, sure, it's...

14:24.860 --> 14:25.880
500 yen.

14:26.160 --> 14:27.060
That's expensive!

14:27.060 --> 14:28.820
Ooh, that's a great deal!

14:28.890 --> 14:30.120
Isn't it, though?

14:31.200 --> 14:32.660
Well, here you go, then.

14:36.070 --> 14:37.930
Do you have the one before this?

14:38.040 --> 14:40.200
What? Um... Um...

14:40.740 --> 14:43.330
I didn't bring 'em today, but I take mail orders.

14:43.640 --> 14:44.700
Give him a flyer.

14:45.180 --> 14:46.240
Flyer?

14:46.310 --> 14:48.250
You see the stack of photocopies there?

14:48.410 --> 14:51.510
It's got info on back issues, and announcements about the next issue.

14:52.050 --> 14:52.850
Wow...

14:52.920 --> 14:54.110
Oh, here you go.

14:54.290 --> 14:56.310
Um, will you take a ske-boo request?

14:56.420 --> 14:57.550
Ske-boo?

14:58.860 --> 15:00.150
Ske-boo...

15:00.560 --> 15:03.430
I'm sorry, we seem to be

15:00.560 --> 15:03.430
out of issues of Ske-boo...

15:02.790 --> 15:04.330
He means

15:02.790 --> 15:04.330
"sketchbook".

15:05.630 --> 15:07.100
Just gimme a second here.

15:19.680 --> 15:20.770
Can't draw?

15:20.850 --> 15:22.580
Yeah, what'll I do?

15:22.880 --> 15:24.180
I'll help you.

15:23.780 --> 15:24.770
What?

15:26.250 --> 15:27.780
Does that look okay to you?

15:28.420 --> 15:31.690
Wow, I didn't know you had such talent, Kazuki.

15:32.890 --> 15:35.380
Do you ever buy comic books?

15:35.790 --> 15:36.850
What?

15:37.060 --> 15:38.430
O-oh, once in a while.

15:38.500 --> 15:41.290
You don't ever get to talk about the story with the artist...

15:41.670 --> 15:44.460
...or have that artist draw a sketch for you like this, right?

15:44.740 --> 15:46.030
Well, of course not.

15:46.200 --> 15:48.100
But, you can do those things here.

15:48.740 --> 15:51.710
All right! There, in color, just for you!

15:54.580 --> 15:56.310
I'll be looking forward to this summer!

15:56.310 --> 15:58.110
I'll have a new issue then, so just you wait!

16:01.020 --> 16:04.290
"Nishimu

16:01.020 --> 16:04.290
This Way"

16:01.690 --> 16:03.290
I missed buying the previous issue.

16:03.290 --> 16:05.790
Wow, the cover with
Multi on it is really cute!

16:04.290 --> 16:06.690
I'll throw in a specially-made laminated card for you this time!

16:07.860 --> 16:09.760
Really? That's so gorgeous!

16:09.330 --> 16:11.500
The Multi cover is really nice.

16:10.930 --> 16:13.200
I'll throw in a specially-made

16:10.930 --> 16:13.200
button this time!

16:12.860 --> 16:14.600
There are even special colors used in this!

16:13.960 --> 16:16.260
I had no idea there was a world like this.

16:16.330 --> 16:17.300
Come on!

16:17.370 --> 16:18.840
We've got customers!

16:18.900 --> 16:21.460
Oh... Yes, how can I help you?

16:22.270 --> 16:26.710
<i>The 6th Spring Comic Fest is now closed.</i>

16:27.210 --> 16:28.810
<i>Those of you with displays,</i>

16:28.810 --> 16:31.540
<i>please have everything</i> <i>cleaned up by 5 o'clock.</i>

16:35.850 --> 16:38.290
We never did find your friend.

16:38.390 --> 16:40.260
Well, it was a good experience anyway.

16:41.690 --> 16:43.830
Well, if luck would have it,
I hope we meet again...

16:43.830 --> 16:45.520
...at some other exhibition and spot sale.

16:52.270 --> 16:53.430
Now...

16:54.870 --> 16:56.770
Hello, my brother.

16:59.640 --> 17:01.340
Where the hell have you...

17:03.050 --> 17:06.510
Come, behold the fruits of today's labor!

17:10.090 --> 17:12.150
The first step towards our ambition is complete.

17:12.290 --> 17:13.880
Let us go home, Comrade Kazuki.

17:14.160 --> 17:16.290
Go home? But what about Mizuki?

17:16.460 --> 17:18.590
Kazuki...

17:24.900 --> 17:25.890
Mizuki!

17:26.070 --> 17:27.540
Kazuki...

17:32.340 --> 17:35.070
Life is wonderful...

17:39.080 --> 17:41.550
A great sacrifice made in the face of our ambition.

17:41.890 --> 17:42.680
Mizuki...

17:43.290 --> 17:44.550
Don't just...

17:44.690 --> 17:46.250
...kill me off!

17:46.790 --> 17:48.280
Why me?

17:53.030 --> 17:55.070
I hate doujinshi.

17:55.070 --> 17:59.530
Hot. Smelly. Noisy. Kazuki. Jerk.

18:00.240 --> 18:02.870
I bet I'm gonna get chewed out later for this.

18:05.940 --> 18:06.970
Good grief.

18:07.080 --> 18:10.670
And it looks like all you wanted was someone to carry your bags.

18:11.550 --> 18:12.880
Do you really believe that?

18:15.550 --> 18:16.850
We're here, Mizuki.

18:17.650 --> 18:18.790
I'm going to bed.

18:18.790 --> 18:19.980
See you later.

18:23.190 --> 18:25.160
I guess it's back to school, starting tomorrow.

18:27.830 --> 18:29.600
What is your problem, Taishi?

18:30.100 --> 18:31.800
Comrade Kazuki!

18:32.400 --> 18:33.930
We have school, starting tomorrow!

18:34.100 --> 18:35.370
Yes! Yes, we do!

18:35.910 --> 18:37.310
But are you satisfied with...

18:37.310 --> 18:39.830
...just letting those ordinary days go by in oblivion?!

18:41.350 --> 18:44.710
Did you not feel it from the people you met today?!

18:52.890 --> 18:55.790
At first, I thought it was a weird place,

18:55.960 --> 18:59.290
but everyone was so enthusiastic, and seemed to be having fun...

18:59.660 --> 19:02.290
Having fun!
Yes, that's it, Comrade Kazuki!

19:02.770 --> 19:04.530
That is what is important!

19:05.070 --> 19:06.040
Huh?

19:06.470 --> 19:07.730
In the 20th century!

19:07.840 --> 19:09.830
The recreational movies developed in
America were exported worldwide...

19:09.910 --> 19:12.140
...and it would not be an exaggeration to say...

19:12.210 --> 19:14.270
...that all the people of Earth were brainwashed...

19:14.340 --> 19:18.250
...with the ideology that could be called entertainment-ism!

19:18.920 --> 19:20.350
And now, in the 21st century!

19:20.480 --> 19:22.540
The new international cultural standard...

19:22.650 --> 19:24.550
...has been sent forth from
Japan to the world!

19:24.660 --> 19:27.020
Yes! That is none other than the doujinshi!

19:28.960 --> 19:31.430
Starting tomorrow, we will be high school seniors.

19:31.700 --> 19:34.670
However, is it fine to proceed with this tranquil life...

19:34.770 --> 19:38.400
...and just automatically graduate up into college?!

19:38.870 --> 19:39.900
Nay!

19:39.900 --> 19:42.100
That is the depravity called stagnation!

19:42.440 --> 19:43.640
What's the commotion about?!

19:43.640 --> 19:45.140
Someone call the police!

19:45.140 --> 19:46.510
You woke up my baby!

19:46.880 --> 19:49.640
World conquest by means of a new media called doujinshi!

19:49.950 --> 19:51.650
True world unification...

19:51.650 --> 19:54.210
...that not even Rome or the great
British Empire was able to achieve!

19:54.320 --> 19:56.480
To become the supreme rulers of the world,

19:56.550 --> 19:59.080
let us now create a doujinshi together!

20:36.790 --> 20:38.920
Good morning, Comrade Kazuki.

20:40.700 --> 20:41.670
Oh.

20:41.730 --> 20:43.430
Have you thought it through?

20:43.700 --> 20:47.470
Well, that is, um, not that you really convinced me,

20:47.540 --> 20:49.100
but maybe if it's just once...

20:49.370 --> 20:50.840
What's just once?

20:51.310 --> 20:52.110
What?!

20:52.840 --> 20:55.570
It bothers me.
What were you talking about?

20:55.780 --> 20:56.970
It's nothing, really.

20:58.480 --> 21:00.280
Come on, hurry up and get to your seats.

21:02.090 --> 21:04.180
Now, before we start homeroom,

21:04.250 --> 21:05.950
I'd like to introduce a transfer student.

21:06.620 --> 21:08.220
What was it about, really?

21:08.530 --> 21:10.060
Well, you know how yesterday...

21:10.060 --> 21:12.620
Hey, you're the guy I met yesterday!

21:12.730 --> 21:14.700
Yeah, from yesterday... What?!

21:17.830 --> 21:19.170
Talk about a coincidence!

21:19.700 --> 21:21.670
Wh-wh-why?!

21:21.670 --> 21:24.470
I'm plannin' on goin' to college over here next year anyway,

21:24.740 --> 21:28.200
so I decided to move in with my relatives a bit early!

21:28.280 --> 21:29.270
You two...

21:32.550 --> 21:33.710
This is truly fate!

21:34.220 --> 21:36.710
All the key players are finally coming together!

21:37.520 --> 21:38.960
Now, all that remains is to draw it!

21:39.490 --> 21:40.680
Comrade Kazuki!

21:41.190 --> 21:42.660
Draw? Draw what?

21:43.230 --> 21:44.160
Why...

21:46.700 --> 21:48.600
What do you think this is?!

21:48.600 --> 21:51.000
What?!

21:53.240 --> 21:56.500
Doujinshi?!

22:20.660 --> 22:24.870
<i>The distant sky looked bright...</i>
<i>Touku no Sora ga Akaruku Mieta</i>

22:24.870 --> 22:29.360
<i>...and we began walking.</i>
<i>Soshite Bokura wa Arukihajimeta</i>

22:29.510 --> 22:33.880
<i>Getting our feet caught in the mud.</i>
<i>Nukarumi ni Ashi o Torarenagara</i>

22:34.080 --> 22:37.950
<i>Heading for a shapeless city.</i>
<i>Katachi no Nai Machi o Mezashite</i>

22:37.950 --> 22:42.090
<i>The pocket in my heart was full...</i>
<i>Kokoro no Naka no Pocket ni wa</i>

22:42.090 --> 22:46.350
<i>...of the grownup things we'd just learned.</i>
<i>Oboetate no Otona ga Ippai</i>

22:46.520 --> 22:50.930
<i>Having taken off our uniforms...</i>
<i>Seifuku o Nuida Bokura ni wa</i>

22:51.060 --> 22:55.100
<i>... the wind was just a little too cold.</i>
<i>Kaze wa Sukoshi Tsumetasugita</i>

22:55.100 --> 22:58.670
<i>Who in the world am I?</i>
<i>Ittai Boku wa Dare Darou</i>

22:58.670 --> 23:03.570
<i>I think about that every so often.</i>
<i>Tokidoki Sonna Koto o Omou</i>

23:03.710 --> 23:07.240
<i>In the world outside the school building...</i>
<i>Kousha no Soto no Sekai de wa</i>

23:07.240 --> 23:12.650
<i>...it's like everyone is a</i> <i>pawn in a game of chess.</i>
<i>Daremo ga Marude Chess no Koma sa</i>

23:13.720 --> 23:18.190
<i>I'm here for you.</i>
<i>Kimi no Tame ni Boku ga Ite</i>

23:18.190 --> 23:22.190
<i>And you for me.</i>
<i>Boku no Tame ni Kimiga</i>

23:22.190 --> 23:26.730
<i>When you think about that...</i>
<i>Sou Omoeba Daremo ga</i>

23:26.730 --> 23:35.700
<i>... everyone is needed by someone.</i>
<i>Dareka no Tame ni Hitsuyou sa</i>

23:56.330 --> 24:20.120
PREVIEW

23:59.160 --> 24:01.530
Our ambition is finally set into motion!

24:01.800 --> 24:04.770
Kazuki successfully creates a masterpiece on his first try!

24:04.770 --> 24:08.170
First edition, 3 million! Sold out!
Cheers! Thank you very much!

24:08.170 --> 24:09.810
Hey, hey, hey, don't just make stuff up!

24:09.810 --> 24:12.910
And so, next time we have a 120 hour special!

24:12.910 --> 24:15.050
Brought to you in 4-dimensional hi-fi sound!

24:15.050 --> 24:17.110
I said, don't make things up!

24:17.980 --> 24:20.310
The real next time, "Put Your Heart Into It."

24:20.380 --> 24:22.890
Can you keep drawing?

24:21.180 --> 24:25.680
NEXT TIME

24:21.180 --> 24:25.680
INTO IT

24:21.180 --> 24:25.680
PUT YOUR HEART

24:22.890 --> 24:24.920
I know I've heard that before somewhere.
